hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15510","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: He informed me, from Uthaym ibn Kulayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have become Muslim, so he said: Cast off from yourself the hair of disbelief, meaning: Shave."
"15511","He said: And another with him informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to another: Cast off from yourself the hair of disbelief, and get circumcised."
